# T5b step 7: refused unauthorized write (design_docs/2026-07-28_turnstone_
# place_port_plan.md, "T5b. Shared address and refused write"). The
# reader joins the place read-only (Invite to place as reader admits at Read
# with no delegation), sees both write permissions read as not effective and
# the founder's one shared node, then attempts to share a node of its own —
# refused by its own worker before anything is authored. Runs as a THIRD
# process launched alongside the relaunched joiner (scenarios/
# place_joiner_return.scn), paired with the founder's continuation in
# scenarios/place_founder.scn through the shared ${EXCHANGE} directory (see
# scenarios/place_two_windows.ps1, which also exports ${EXCHANGE_URL}).
settle 30
key escape

# Wait for the founder's second (reader) card before offering a pre-key
# against it.
wait-file 3000 ${EXCHANGE}\demo-reader.place-card.json

act Offer place pre-key
settle 5
type ${EXCHANGE}\demo-reader.place-card.json
key enter
settle 10
wait-file 600 ${EXCHANGE}\demo-reader.place-card.json.prekey.json

# Wait for the founder's reader invitation (naming this pre-key) before
# joining.
wait-file 3000 ${EXCHANGE}\demo-reader.place-card.json.prekey.json.invite.json

act Join place
settle 5
type ${EXCHANGE}\demo-reader.place-card.json.prekey.json.invite.json
key enter
settle 10
wait-status 600 Local rendezvous

# Admitted at Read with no delegation: the shared-graph write permission
# reads as not effective, and the founder's one shared node has already
# synced in through ordinary graph sync by the time this settles.
wait-status 600 Shared graph permission: not effective
wait-status 6000 Retained history: 1 shared nodes

# Open the OTHER page (never the founder's shared address) and attempt to
# share it; this profile's own worker must refuse before anything is
# authored.
open ${EXCHANGE_URL}/reader.html
settle 20
act Toggle live content
settle 30
assert content-ready
assert content-live
act Open node in Workbench
settle 30
assert pane workbench
assert surface content
capture reader_page

act Share focused node
settle 30
assert event place-refused

# Still one shared node: the refused write added nothing.
wait-status 60 Retained history: 1 shared nodes

act Place status
settle 10
capture reader_refused
record-place reader
# The status view stays open after its capture, and the next press only
# dismisses it; close it before any row click below.
key escape
settle 5

# Signal the founder that this leg is complete; the founder is waiting on
# this marker before it opens and shares its Knot document (T5c) below, so
# this leg must run BEFORE that, not after.
touch ${EXCHANGE}\reader.finished

# T5c (design_docs/2026-07-28_turnstone_place_port_plan.md, "T5c. Shared
# Knot document by projection"): attempt to visit the founder's Knot
# document once it is shared. A reader carries no projection-connect grant
# (Invite to place as reader issues no delegation), so the dial is refused
# at the door and the node is kept, refused, exactly as the graph write
# above. The founder shares this node only after seeing reader.finished
# above, so wait for the shared-node count to grow before looking for the
# row; the exact knot:// address (the founder's root hex) is never known to
# this scenario in advance.
wait-status 6000 Retained history: 2 shared nodes
# The Roster (not Trail) lists every graph node regardless of local
# navigation history; this node arrived purely through sync (run 17 found
# trail/roster/inspector/arrange all reporting empty with no list pane open).
act Open Roster pane
settle 20
wait-row 600 field.knot
# Both `click-row field.knot` (DOM class-selector) and a coordinate `click-at`
# read off an actual capture of this exact state (run 20's `reader_knot_debug`,
# which shows the row rendered at this position) missed identically: focus
# stayed on "Reader page" either way, while the identical click-row verb
# worked for the returning joiner against a shorter Roster. Give the newly
# inserted row extra settle time between wait-row's success and the click, in
# case the DOM has not caught up with the observation the same frame.
settle 20
click-row field.knot
settle 20
assert focused field.knot
capture reader_knot_debug
# Merely opening/selecting the node does not by itself attempt the dial
# (run 18 found this: no toggle meant no dial, so `knot_documents` stayed
# empty and the refusal was never recorded). Toggling live content is what
# makes the app actually try to mount the document, which is refused at the
# door for a reader; do not assert content-live here, unlike the founder and
# the returning joiner, since a refusal is exactly what this leg expects.
act Toggle live content
settle 30
assert event place-refused
wait-knot 600 refused
record-place reader_knot

# Let the founder know this leg is done too. This must complete while the
# founder is still alive to refuse the dial, so the founder waits on this
# marker (beside knot.done) before it exits.
touch ${EXCHANGE}\reader_knot.finished

log place reader refused-write path complete
